  "interpretations": [
    "At 8 clients, 10800s improves CPU/request 3.9%-6.7% and throughput 3.6%-6.3%, with low p50 baseline drift; does not improve every tail: pod_namespace 8-client p99 300.3555->303.7415ms (regression 1.1%).",
    "node_broad at 4 clients p50 537.73->466.94ms (13.2%) but A/A drift is 21.39%; cannot claim robust p50 speedup from that case.",
    "pod_broad 4/8 clients CPU decreases 7.3%/5.4% with 0.38%/0.67% baseline CPU control drift; stronger within-run evidence.",
    "SelectedMarks node 117->53, pod_namespace229->82, pod_broad233->82. Selected marks and read rows are physical-read effects, NOT proof of mutex contention.",
    "RSS under separate fresh processes plus an approximate 4Hz sampler is not enough to claim allocator-specific memory savings."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Synthetic aligned 3h node lifetimes, three days only; no staggered node start, realistic HPA, 14d, stale/NaN/ACL controls.",
    "Read-only fixed one-part dataset; no simultaneous continuous ingest and merges.",
    "Only one runner and one repeat of 9 ABBA combinations; p99 is a noisy tail estimate.",
    "Lab binary glibc O1; not production jemalloc or production O2.",
    "OSCPUWait is runnable scheduler wait, not a contended mutex; inferred pool-lock effects are tiny and unstable."
  ],
  "next_action": "Validate staggered node-start fixture SHA and actual bucket occupancy with same source and O1 binary; compare 3600 versus10800 at unchanged 1d native selectors and controls to bound sensitivity to bucket alignment before promotion."
